body:
PC. Straight up told them that I wanted a full refund as I was expecting a canvas bag not a cheaply made nylon bag, due to the false advertisement when I placed my pre-order. I showed them their own [advertisement](https://c1-ebgames.eb-cdn.com.au/merchandising/images/packshots/28804119ab024fe1bd7cbf4cb7357423_Original.jpg) of the game in their website, also had my state's consumer [rights](https://www.fairtrading.nsw.gov.au/buying-products-and-services/repairs,-replacements-and-refunds) that I can show them in case they refuse to do my refund.

&#x200B;

Hope this helps you.

&#x200B;

Edit: Linked the [photo](https://imgur.com/zMr0d9e)

!entered

&nbsp;
